      "title": "Captions start in sync but drift out later?",
      "copy": "Captions start in sync but drift out later? Check three points before shifting the whole subtitle file.\n\n• Same delay at the start, middle and end: a constant offset may help. If every cue is 1.5 seconds late, shift by −1.5 seconds, then review.\n\n• Delay grows as the video plays: one constant offset will not fix the drift. Check that the subtitles match the video version and timing.\n\n• A sudden jump after a cut: check that edit before moving every cue.\n\nKeep the original file and spot-check the export against your video.\n\nCaption Cleanup Kit is my offline tool for existing SRT/VTT files. It applies a constant timing offset and can convert subtitle formats or export transcripts. US$9 once, with a quick-start guide and samples. It does not transcribe audio or automatically repair timing drift.\n\nhttps://tiaanbok0.gumroad.com/l/caption-cleanup-kit?utm_source=facebook&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=timingtip20261008",
